First Samurai ascension.
Only one death between my barbarian ascension and this one(lously
loadstones...)


My dog was killed by a rock trap on lvl 1, not a good start...

Found a blessed lamp on level 1, too bad it was oil.  Luckily
another(magic one) was found on the way to minetown.  Altar was co-
aligned.  After some typos and waiting and sacrificing, I was granted
a wish and got GDSM.  Sacrifices also produced Snickersnee, which I
used until the castle.

In the mines I worked up long sword to E, then dual wielded with my
other katana, which eventually I also worked up to E.  I used the bow
in the early game for eyes and other appropriate long range
situations.  Finally, I should note that there were many polytraps on
one of the levels.  I was able to kill a golden naga and got poison
resistance along with a lich, which just scared the bejeesus out of
me.  I got the luckstone and some potions from the cellar, and moved
on.

No bones files this time, but I made it through sokoban and got a
BoH.  Like previous games, this dungeon was LOADED with altars.  Some
were co-aligned, but I converted most of the others just for grins.
Some decent stores were found, but in particular the jewelry store was
HUGE.  Probably 50 rings and 2 amulets.  I got lucky with a scroll of
identify while holding as much of his stock as I could carry.  I
puchased slow digestion, regeneration, free action, conflict, and
levitation.

By this time, I had a lot of potions, so time for alchemy.  Smokey was
healing, so that nerfed a bit of my alchemy, but I did get a wish, and
went for speed boots(maybe reflection would have been a better wish).

I found enough vaults and leprechan halls to fill my pockets, so I
maxed out protection and gave up the search for Ludios.  I ate corpses
for intrinsics, getting my last one on medusa by using magical
breathing and eating electric eel corpses.

Used mastermind to open the castle and crush a good bit of monsters.
Cleaned up the rest and got the wand.  No good equipment in the
castle, but I did already find a helm of telepathy, so I stuck with
that.  I wished for a cloak of protections, amulet of reflection,
gauntlets of power.I had found a magic marker, so charging wasn't a
problem.  I saved the other two wishes.

Did the quest with no real problems.  Found two more magic markers.
At that point I was foo resistant, well protected, and was generally
ready for late game.  I decided to go for the gusto and wish for Frost
Brand, but the wish failed.  I would imagine it was because my quest
artificact counts for wishing purposes?  I guess I thought it would be
guaranteed since I was only counting Snickersnee.  Can someone
enlighten me?

I used my last wish for 2 scrolls of genocide since I had not found
them yet.  Only got 1 and used it on L.  I sat on a throne(maybe in
the castle) and was granted a wish, which I used again for Frost Brand
and got it.  Additionally, I polypiled my unicorn horns and got
another marker and found a Hawaiian shirt.  That got me to about
-44AC, +6 FB and +7 katana.  The rest was a piece of cake.

I wrote some more genocide and got rid of V and m.  Payed off demons
and killed the others.  More alchemy got me up to 250+HP.  I also
wrote magic mapping scrolls and mapped all levels to save time.  I had
3 death wands by the time I marked the square(at dlvl 52, ugh).
Killed Rodney, went to the sanctum.  A little trouble there, as some
priests summoned insects a few times, but I chased them down quickly
and finished them off.  Took the amulet, but Moloch tried to blast me,
which I don't remember in other games...

Got cursed a lot, but not too many Rodney sightings.  My only worry
was that I never found gold detection.  I did find a single scroll on
about dlvl 4 or 5, but I couldn't write enough.  Luckily near that
shop was another with a crystal ball that I overlooked.  I had to mill
around and find a mummy wrapping to get in.  In general I wasted a lot
of time dipping potions and getting stuff rather than escaping.

Finally made it to the planes and killed Rodney for the last time.
Used the crystal ball on Earth, Fire, and Water(only had 3 charges).
I made some educated guesses and used wand of secret door detection on
Air.  Malignant aura cursed my katana on Water, and I almost lost the
dang thing.  Also, because of smokey=3Dhealing, I had a lot of gain
level potions left over, so I quaffed them all, hence the high
character level.  After much difficulty, I made it to Astral.

I took on Famine first(on the right).  Super, super easy compared to
other runs.  Priests seemed to refuse to summon insects.  I killed
them and the angels quickly.  I did mean I had to fight Famine a few
times because he had a clear line on me.  I meleed him to death the
2nd time, he never got a hit in.  I went into the inner chamber and
cleared out the angels and priests there as well.  The altar was
lawful(whew).

I was not actually overflowing with wishes this time, but I had
plenty.  I was very hesitant to play Samurai because I didn't
understand the conduct.  It was never a problem for me, and I loved
the quest.






